# ORIGINAL: FLIAPI's mutant list — no swipl-devel counterpart.
# tools/mutants/FLIAPI.py — the mutation battery of FLI-API group 1 (audit D-0777 (4)(a)): the pl-fli.c API functions
# PL_put_bool, PL_put_pointer, PL_put_functor, PL_put_list, PL_get_uintptr, PL_get_pointer, PL_get_arg
# (PL_get_arg_sz), PL_get_compound_name_arity (PL_get_compound_name_arity_sz), PL_unify_int64_ex, PL_unify_pointer
# (src/pl-fli.jl), and of group 2: PL_new_atom, PL_new_atom_mbchars, PL_new_functor_sz, PL_new_functor, PL_functor_name,
# PL_functor_arity, PL_atom_chars, PL_atom_nchars, PL_atom_wchars, PL_atom_mbchars, PL_get_atom_chars (ids N, M, F, R, C,
# W, G, B), run ONCE, in CI (.github/workflows/mutation.yml; locally: tools/mutate.sh run). Format:
# tools/mutate_drive.py's (as ARGINL.py): `id`, `file`, `old` (must occur EXACTLY once), `new`, optional `equivalent`
# and `targets`. Each id is AIMED BY the rows its "aimed by" names, all in test/core_lang/test_fli_api1_cells.jl. Verdicts:
# written by the battery, not yet run. Every `old` was counted in src/pl-fli.jl at the commit that added this list
# (a text count, no Julia): each occurs exactly once.
# TARGETS (audit D-0238): the new functions have no caller in the kernel yet (foreign code calls them), so the step's own
# file is the only one that exercises the mutated code; PL_unify_int64_ex and PL_unify_pointer reach unify_int64_ex, whose
# other callers' file test_fli_unify_cells.jl is listed too.
# GROUP E1 (ids E1-E29): PL_put_atom_chars, PL_put_atom_nchars, PL_put_string_chars, PL_put_string_nchars, PL_put_chars,
# PL_put_list_ncodes, PL_put_list_codes, PL_put_list_nchars, PL_put_list_chars, PL_unify_atom_chars, PL_unify_atom_nchars,
# PL_unify_string_chars, PL_unify_string_nchars, PL_unify_list_ncodes, PL_unify_list_codes, PL_unify_list_nchars,
# PL_unify_list_chars (PL_unify_chars is wip/clib-uri's and wip/clib1's) and the helpers _fli_chars_text and _latin1_string; no row feeds invalid UTF-8
# (the canonicalisation failure of PL_put_chars' PL_ATOM, `false`, has no mutant), nor a 0 byte to PL_put_list_nchars
# (codeToAtom refuses it).
# GROUP E2 (ids E37-E56 and E61-E66; E30-E36 and E57-E60 aimed at wip/clib-uri's PL_unify_chars, PL_unify_wchars(_diff), PL_get_wchars: removed): PL_cvt_encoding, _PL_cvt_i_char
# (PL_cvt_i_schar, PL_cvt_i_uchar), _PL_cvt_i_short, PL_cvt_i_int64, PL_cvt_i_uint64 (and its helper _fli_get_uint64_ex),
# PL_get_list_nchars, PL_get_nchars, PL_get_chars, uncachedCodeToAtom, codeToAtom. NOT LISTED: cleanupCodeToAtom (a no-op: no
# state), and the PL_STRINGS_MARK / PL_save_text buffer code (left out). The codeToAtom ids use TC: char_code/2 and
# PL_unify_text's lists reach it.
# GROUP 3 (ids H1-H12): PL_context, PL_new_module, PL_pred, PL_predicate, PL_predicate_info (resolveModule is wip/clib1's); PL_context's
# frame branch (the context module of an environment frame) has no row: no frame is open in the test's engine.
# NOT LISTED (group 2): the canonicalisation failure of PL_new_atom_mbchars (no input of the two encodings it takes
# fails: `nothing` is upstream's 0 for a wide text with an invalid code point) and the `$expr` branch of PL_functor_name.
# NOT LISTED: PL_put_list's and PL_put_functor's cell COUNT (the compound's arity is its functor word; a missing cell
# would be read past, a garbage read, not a verdict).
# GROUP D (ids D1-D29): blob_write_usc_atom, initUCSAtoms, isUCSAtom, get_atom_ptr_text, get_atom_text, get_string_text,
# compareUCSAtom, saveUCSAtom, loadUCSAtom, is_text_value, get_value_text, PL_get_text_as_atom (and its helpers _fli_text_codes,
# _fli_text_has_nul). NOT LISTED: the canonicalisation and textToAtom failure branches of PL_get_text_as_atom (PL_get_text never
# gives an invalid code point), the blob type's register call is D28 (a candidate equivalent).
